// (docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_A2.md, row m16 = m8: PROJ KIRJ RÄÄK LUGE, with the leads of modules 11–19; gates
// V1–V16 of docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_B1.md §8). One storyline, September, a year before the B1 course (docs/COURSE_CAST.md). Sofia started at
// Tuul Logistika on Wednesday 1 September (boss Liis Laan, colleagues Anna and Markus; June–August at Kaubahall, before that two years in a Tartu bookshop).
// The autumn course at Keelekool Sõna starts on Monday 6 September (Maret, Aune, administrator Ene; Tom, Lucía, Dmitri, Olga). The module product: the
// Lugude õhtu („story evening”) in Jaan's café Pann on Friday 24 September at 18; rehearsal with Aune on Monday 13 September. Sofia's bad Tuesday 7 September:
// bus 6, rain, the bag falls, a blue folder stays on the bus, late for Liis's meeting. Pictures of the Kasuta sheets (art/visuals/a2-module-16.js):
// 076 Jaan's cards of yesterday, 077 Sofia shows Anna the pictures, 080 Anna and Markus put the weekend pictures in order.
//   076 PROJ L→S  the simple past and ei + nud (olin, tulin, läksin, tegin, sain, nägin); corner L1 (short notices, multiple choice); main: the pair
//                 chooses their stories for the evening (S03).
//   077 KIRJ L→W  a recent event in order (kõigepealt, siis, pärast seda, äkki, õnneks, lõpuks); corner S1 (picture and questions, S06, in Kasuta);
//                 main: a 60–80-word text „Mis eile juhtus?” (W05), planned and edited.
//   078 RÄÄK R→S  a short story in the past (kes, kus, millal, mis juhtus, miks; the found letter in the Tartu bookshop); corner W2a (a message, W02);
//                 main: the learner tells their own story (S02); S05 = `078_p_cards`.
//   079 LUGE R→W  experience: olen käinud, ei ole käinud, Kas sa oled kunagi …? against the simple past with a time; corner R2 (sentences ↔ three
//                 texts); main: a 50–70-word letter to the school paper (W08).
//   080 PROOV     Mock 2: all four parts timed (B.examPart); tasks tagged R1–R5, L1–L4, W1, W2a, W2b, S0, S1, S2. Writing + reading on Harjuta,
//                 listening + speaking on Kasuta.
// Every teaching lesson: „Mäletad?” naming the previous lesson and one of modules 12–14, an in-lesson pair task, a home recording in Kasuta, two fluency
// tasks, one exam corner. No tingiv kõneviis (A2).
